// Settings > Display > Black frame insertion: a black frame shown between normal ones on
// screens running at 100 Hz or more, after PakoVM's BFI app (MIT, see NOTICE). The display
// controller does the black frames (kernel rockchip_drm_vop.c, bfi parameter); this is the
// settings page. The entry only shows while Peak refresh rate is 100 Hz or more; Settings
// and the boot receiver switch it on and off. System user, to write the parameter.
android_app {
    name: "BlackFrameInsertion",
    srcs: ["src/**/*.java"],
    resource_dirs: ["res"],
    certificate: "platform",
    platform_apis: true,
    optimize: {
        enabled: false,
    },
}
